.TH pvc-filter 1  "pvc-filter " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-filter \- Fixed\-spectrum phase\-vocoder filter: multiplies each frame\*(Aqs amplitude by a shaped copy of a `.fr` response, then mixes the filtered signal with (unless disabled) the original source
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-filter\fR <\fB\-\-response\fR> [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-stretch\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-freq\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-time\-delay\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\-time\-scaler\fR] [\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-freq\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-time\-delay\fR] [\fB\-\-response\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-response\-freq\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-response\-warp\fR] [\fB\-\-response\-smoothing\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-floor\fR] [\fB\-\-pitch\-shift\-source\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-band\-reject\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-comp\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-comp\-amount\fR] [\fB\-\-expand\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-expand\-amount\fR] [\fB\-\-normalization\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-normalize\-to\-response\fR] [\fB\-\-attack\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fixed\-spectrum phase\-vocoder filter: multiplies each frame\*(Aqs amplitude by a shaped copy of a `.fr` response, then mixes the filtered signal with (unless disabled) the original source.
.PP
Ports `filter`\*(Aqs audio\-processing path (`legacy/pvc_src/ filter.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools::filter`\*(Aqs doc comment for what\*(Aqs in and out of scope (oscillator\-bank resynthesis \- needed only for pitch/frequency\-shifted output \- isn\*(Aqt ported yet).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-response\fR \fI<RESPONSE>\fR
Path to the `.fr` response file (its own size determines the FFT size \- see `pvc\-core::tools::filter`\*(Aqs doc comment)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 2048]
Analysis/resynthesis window length. `0` means auto (`2 * fft`); the C\*(Aqs own hardcoded default is a literal `2048`, matching `pv`\*(Aqs `\-\-window\-size` gotcha
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]

.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]

.TP
\fB\-\-stretch\fR \fI<STRETCH>\fR [default: 1]
Time\-stretch factor (`1.0` = unchanged)
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-pitch\fR \fI<FILTER_PITCH>\fR [default: 0]
Filter\-output pitch shift in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-freq\-shift\fR \fI<FILTER_FREQ_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
Filter\-output frequency shift in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-gain\fR \fI<FILTER_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Filter\-output gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-time\-delay\fR \fI<FILTER_TIME_DELAY>\fR [default: 0]
Filter\-output time delay in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\-time\-scaler\fR \fI<DELAY_TIME_SCALER>\fR [default: 1]
Scales the effective delay used when resolving time\-varying parameters against a delayed frame \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE_ENABLED>\fR [default: true]
Mix the (delayed/shifted) original source in alongside the filtered signal \- on by default, matching the real tool (see `pvc\-core::tools::filter`\*(Aqs doc comment)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-gain\fR \fI<SOURCE_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Source gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-pitch\fR \fI<SOURCE_PITCH>\fR [default: 0]
Source pitch shift in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-freq\-shift\fR \fI<SOURCE_FREQ_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
Source frequency shift in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-time\-delay\fR \fI<SOURCE_TIME_DELAY>\fR [default: 0]
Source time delay in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-response\-pitch\fR \fI<RESPONSE_PITCH>\fR [default: 0]
Response pitch shift in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-response\-freq\-shift\fR \fI<RESPONSE_FREQ_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
Response frequency shift in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-response\-warp\fR \fI<RESPONSE_WARP>\fR [default: 0]
Response magnitude warp index \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-response\-smoothing\fR \fI<RESPONSE_SMOOTHING>\fR [default: 0]
Response smoothing bandwidth: positive is Hz, negative is octaves \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-floor\fR \fI<SOURCE_FLOOR>\fR [default: \-96]
Source signal floor in dB \- how much of the source passes through unfiltered at the response\*(Aqs quietest points \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-pitch\-shift\-source\-only\fR
Apply the filter output\*(Aqs own pitch/frequency shift only to the source, not to how the response is positioned (off by default: the response tracks the filter output\*(Aqs shift too)
.TP
\fB\-\-band\-reject\fR
Invert the response (band\-reject instead of band\-pass)
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_FREQ>\fR [default: 200]

.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_FREQ>\fR [default: 2000]

.TP
\fB\-\-comp\-threshold\fR \fI<COMP_THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0]
Compression threshold in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-comp\-amount\fR \fI<COMP_AMOUNT>\fR [default: 0]
Compression amount in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-expand\-threshold\fR \fI<EXPAND_THRESHOLD>\fR [default: \-96]
Expansion threshold in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-expand\-amount\fR \fI<EXPAND_AMOUNT>\fR [default: 0]
Expansion amount in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-normalization\-limit\fR \fI<NORMALIZATION_LIMIT>\fR [default: 0]
Per\-frame amplitude normalization limit in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-normalize\-to\-response\fR
Normalize each frame to match the filter response\*(Aqs own loudness instead of the (delayed) input sound\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-attack\fR \fI<ATTACK>\fR [default: 0]
Envelope attack time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR [default: 0]
Envelope release time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

